    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "For example, if Γ0 = Zd, then EΓ0(θ) = 2 di=1 cos2πθi and if Γ0 is the triangular lattice, then EΓ0(θ) = 2cos2πθ1 + 2cos2πθ2 + 2cos2π(θ1 + θ2), for θi ∈ [0,1). Here Γ1,2,3 are viewed as periodic graphs with fundamental domain containing νF vertices, cf. [7, Lemma 3.1, §3.4], with (vi) the vertices of GF."
